Report: Exact integer generation, seed initialization and state restoration in Rand32 and Rand64
12 claims; 0 removal(s).
  run_ids: ["d968322a-8abb-4ff3-a696-3242aa92dff6"] -> ["1a8a39c6-536f-47b0-8ae3-6451e63b7fbf"]
  title: "Exact next-word output and state update in Rand32" -> "Exact integer generation, seed initialization and state restoration in Rand32 and Rand64"
  explanation: "For the unchanged Rand32::rand_u32 body, every u64 state s and increment i returns the PCG-XSH-RR output rotate_right(low32(((s >> 18) XOR s) >> 27), low32(s >> 59)), and updates the state to (6364136223846793005*s+i) modulo 2^64 while preserving the increment. Right shifts are logical. The call terminates without model failure. Original crate Rust source and Cargo manifest are unchanged; official Aeneas scalar and array primitives supply all library operations, without custom external models." -> "For oorandom 11.1.5, twelve unchanged APIs have exact value/state proofs: new, new_inc, state, from_state, the unsigned output method and the signed output method for both Rand32 and Rand64. For arbitrary seed and increment input, new_inc normalizes the stream to ((increment << 1) OR 1), starts at zero, performs one PCG state update, adds the seed modulo the state width, then performs a second PCG state update. new uses the published DEFAULT_INC. state returns the exact current state and increment, and from_state restores those values unchanged; two additional composition theorems establish save/restore identity. Unsigned generation returns the exact PCG-XSH-RR output permutation of the old state and advances to multiplier*state+increment modulo 2^64 or 2^128. Signed generation preserves that updated state and reinterprets the unsigned result bits as i32 or i64. Each covered call terminates normally in the Aeneas model for every scalar input, including zero states and even restored increments."
  trusted_assumptions: "The Rust compiler, Charon/Aeneas translation, official Aeneas scalar/array models and Lean kernel are trusted. Standard-library operator implementations are modeled by the official Aeneas library, rather than individually body-proved. The public theorem has no extra local axioms; transitive dependencies allow only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound." -> "The Rust compiler, official Charon/Aeneas translation, official Aeneas scalar models and Lean kernel are trusted. No custom external models or local trusted helper contracts are used. All fourteen public and supplementary theorem dependency audits permit only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. Standard-library wrapping, casts, shifts and rotations use official Aeneas models, rather than body proofs of Rust std implementations."
  environment: "Rust nightly-2026-09-17; Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f; official Aeneas frontend/library be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a; Lean 4.35.0. Targeted original-body extraction via official --start-from. Source/archive hashes, regenerated translation comparison, tests and transitive axiom audit are retained in evidence." -> "Original crates.io oorandom 11.1.5 src/Cargo.toml, archive-compared without changes. Rust nightly-2026-09-17; Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f; official Aeneas frontend/library be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a; Lean 4.35.0. Official targeted extraction selects all twelve original bodies and their shared callees. Original tests, regeneration hashes and integrated Lean/axiom audits are retained in evidence."
  evidence_url: "https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/tree/db2a5c20a4999ca201db13c682ee3d2699790bda" -> "https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/tree/a533a3edfd8327d552e2b072773161dc4408e27e"
  limitations: "Only Rand32::rand_u32 is verified, for the default feature configuration on x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu. Seed constructors, state access/restoration, other generators, signed/floating/ranged output, advancement, buffer filling, serialization and inherited wrappers are outside this proof. No period, distribution, independence, nonzero-state invariant or cryptographic property is established." -> "The proof covers twelve integer/state APIs on x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu with the original default configuration. rand_float and rand_range for both generators remain unproved, as do non-excluded inherited/default and external blanket methods. The save/restore composition theorem establishes pure state identity; no arbitrary user callback or destructor behavior is modeled. No period, statistical distribution, independence or cryptographic guarantee is established. Other targets were not checked."
